55
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.798
In contrast, an instruction-tuned
LLM, which is where a lot of

56
00:02:59.798 --> 00:03:03.524
momentum of LLM research and
practice has been going, an

57
00:03:03.524 --> 00:03:07.623
instruction-tuned LLM has been trained to
follow instructions. So, if you

58
00:03:07.623 --> 00:03:12.467
were to ask it what is
the capital of France, it's much more

59
00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:15.448
likely to output something
like, the capital of

60
00:03:15.448 --> 00:03:19.546
France is Paris. So the way
that instruction-tuned LLMs are typically

61
00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:22.527
trained is you start
off with a base

62
00:03:22.527 --> 00:03:27.744
LLM that's been trained on a
huge amount of text data and further train

63
00:03:27.744 --> 00:03:31.842
it, further fine-tune it with inputs
and outputs that are instructions

64
00:03:31.842 --> 00:03:34.078
and good attempts
to follow those

65
00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:37.804
instructions, and then often further refine
using a technique called

66
00:03:37.804 --> 00:03:40.412
RLHF, reinforcement learning
from human feedback, to

67
00:03:40.412 --> 00:03:43.766
make the system better
able to be helpful and

68
00:03:43.766 --> 00:03:46.747
follow instructions. Because instruction-tuned
LLMs have been trained

69
00:03:46.747 --> 00:03:48.982
to be
helpful, honest, and harmless,

70
00:03:48.982 --> 00:03:52.708
so for example, they are
